# No merge driver, on purpose.
#
# A driver here applies to a merge git performs and to nothing else. GitHub reads none of them:
# neither the mergeability it reports on a pull request nor the merge its button performs consults
# one. So a driver is in force exactly where nobody is looking and absent where everybody is, and
# the file it is meant to keep mergeable reads as conflicting on every pull request open across
# another one's merge — while `git merge` on a clone resolves it silently, which is what keeps the
# report from being believed.
#
# Both files that had one — `CHANGELOG.md` and `DEFECTS.md` — record a change in a file of its own
# now, under `changelog/` and `defects/`, so two branches never write the same line and there is
# nothing for either merge to resolve. That is the fix a driver could only paper over locally.
#
# `docs.rs::no_merge_driver_is_what_keeps_two_branches_apart` asserts this file names none, because
# the reliance is easier to add back than to notice.
